# run.py BITSTREAM TEXT...: load into SRAM with openFPGALoader -b ulx3s, then open
# /dev/cu.usbserial-<FTDI-serial>, type each TEXT, print what came back within 0.5 s.

# A first try opened the port before the load, to catch the banner. The loader
# then failed: "unable to open ftdi device: -5 (unable to claim usb device. Make
# sure the default FTDI driver is not in use)". JTAG and the UART share the
# FT231X, so nothing was loaded and the flash design kept running.

# Official bitstream (committed firmware), 2026-11-08T20:05:29Z
loader exit: 0 | ['SRAM erase: DONE', 'Disable configuration: DONE']
on opening: b''
typed b'hi\r' -> b'HI\r\n> '
typed b'Hello, ULX3S\r' -> b'HELLO, ULX3S\r\n> '

